# User data lives in the working directory, never in the plugin
workspaces/
inputs/
.pane/
gate-app.json
.social-pipeline/
.creative-discovery/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
scripts/test/.out/

# Internal planning and review documents stay local. Everything listed below ships,
# because something depends on it: agents read SHARED-RULES.md at runtime, a test reads
# the source tables and THIRD_PARTY_SOURCES.md, the README links the architecture, flow
# and attribution files, and AUTHORING.md is how the next person adds a skill without
# guessing the house style. The .excalidraw is the diagram's source, so it can be edited
# later rather than redrawn.
docs/*
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/FLOW.md
!docs/ATTRIBUTION.md
!docs/THIRD_PARTY_SOURCES.md
!docs/AUTHORING.md
!docs/SHARED-RULES.md
!docs/STAGES.md
!docs/PRESENTATION.md
!docs/assets/
!docs/3echo-social-campaign-flow.html
!docs/3echo-social-campaign-product-doc.html
!docs/publishing-backend.md
# The defect log ships because trace-run.js tells whoever reads it to add a row, and a
# log that only exists on one machine cannot stop a defect coming back on another.
!docs/RUN-DEFECTS.md
# The function-hooks plan ships because the agents implementing it read it from here,
# and the probes it names write their answers into RUN-DEFECTS.md beside it.
!docs/FUNCTION-HOOKS-PLAN.md
# The media pricing contract ships because make-video and SHARED-RULES.md both send the run
# to it at the moment it is about to quote somebody a number.
!docs/PRICING.md
!docs/sources/
!docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE_FLOW.png
!docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE_FLOW.excalidraw
# The pannable execution map. Self-contained, no network, and the README links it.
!docs/EXECUTION-MAP.html
!docs/CURRENT-FLOW.html
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
